module bindings.c.dest_capacity_member_array;

// A struct that declares one of its fields as an array of constant size has
// stated that field's capacity in the one place it can be stated, so a
// byte-count transfer into that field is bounded by the declaration and by
// nothing else. A count taken from elsewhere -- a length read off the wire, a
// value a caller hands over -- is bounded by wherever it came from, and a
// function that never compares that count has no bound on the write at all:
// the transfer runs past the member array exactly when the count is the larger
// of the two. The declaration is what makes this a small set, which is why the
// count is required to be a bare identifier the body never relates to anything
// rather than any transfer into any field.
//
// The fact is emitted by the C frontend
// (ccDestCapacityMemberArrayObservations,
// internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go) from the syntax tree and is
// callee-neutral, carrying the argument position the member array occupies so
// that which spellings count as transfers, and which of their arguments is the
// destination, is decided here in data: the two C standard byte-copy
// primitives and documented library aliases of the same signature take the
// destination first (pjlib's pj_memcpy, SDL's SDL_memcpy), while the dissector
// toolkit's bulk-copy primitive takes it second -- tvb_memcpy copies `length`
// bytes at `offset` into `target` and, per its own header comment, "assumes
// that the target memory is already allocated; it does not allocate or free
// the target memory", a byte-count copy into a destination whose capacity the
// caller must know. Keeping the position here rather than in the engine is
// what stops a transfer that reads from a member array from being read as one
// that writes into it.
//
// Residuals, all false-negative: the count is the call's last argument, so a
// spelling that follows it with a flags word is not paired; a destination or
// count wrapped in a cast is not paired; and a bound enforced in the caller of
// a helper is invisible to the helper's own body.
binding destCapacityMemberArray {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.kind == "any" and node.analysis == "copy.member_capacity_unchecked" and containsAny(node.token, ["arg0=memcpy", "arg0=memmove", "arg0=pj_memcpy", "arg0=SDL_memcpy", "arg1=tvb_memcpy"])
  emit issue code.DestCapacityUncheckedCopy at node
}
